DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     mmaakkee is a program designed to simplify the maintenance of other programs.
     Its input is a _m_a_k_e_f_i_l_e: a list of specifications (target rules) describ‐
     ing build relationships between programs and other files.  By default,
     the file _m_a_k_e_f_i_l_e is used; if no such file is found, it tries _M_a_k_e_f_i_l_e.
     If neither of these exist, mmaakkee can still rely on a set of built-in sys‐
     tem rules.

     If the file ‘_._d_e_p_e_n_d’ exists, it will also be read after the main
     _m_a_k_e_f_i_l_e (see mkdep(1)).

     The handling of ‘_._d_e_p_e_n_d’ is a BSD extension.

     If a list of _t_a_r_g_e_t _._._. is specified, mmaakkee will build those targets.
     Otherwise a default target will be built: either a target explicitly
     marked with ..MMAAIINN or the first target encountered in the _m_a_k_e_f_i_l_e.

