SSPPEECCIIAALL PPRREERREEQQUUIISSIITTEESS
     Of the special targets described in the previous section, the ones that
     tag prerequisites can also be used as prerequisites, in which case the
     corresponding targets will be tagged accordingly.

     This is an extension, even for standard special targets.

     mmaakkee also recognizes some other prerequisites:

     ..NNOOTTMMAAIINN   Normally mmaakkee selects the first target it encounters as the
                default target to be built if no target was specified.  This
                prerequisite prevents this target from being selected.

     ..OOPPTTIIOONNAALL  If a target is marked with this attribute and mmaakkee can't fig‐
                ure out how to create it, it will ignore this fact and assume
                the file isn't needed or already exists.

     ..UUSSEE       Turn the target into mmaakkee's version of a macro.  When the tar‐
                get is used as a prerequisite for another target, the other
                target acquires the commands, prerequisites, and attributes
                (except for ..UUSSEE) of the prerequisite.  If the target already
                has commands, the ..UUSSEE target's commands are appended to them.

     ..WWAAIITT      If ..WWAAIITT appears in a dependency line, the prerequisites that
                precede it are made before the prerequisites that follow it in
                the line.  Loops are not detected and targets that form loops
                will be silently ignored.

